          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 9162.5,
            "y": 9478
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_NER_RESOLUTION_AGENT",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1768234432577",
          "id": "1765361904570",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1765361904572_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Set NER_Status as {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_VERIFY_NER_RESULT.$output.result}}.\n- Input message: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_CONTEXT_REWRITER_NODE.$output.rewrittenRequest}}\n- Chat history: {{$context.$system.$chatHistory}}\n- Ambiguous message:  {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_GET_REQUESTED_ARTIFACT_DETAILS.$output.ambiguousMessage}} \n\nIf NER_Status.hasNERError is true, proceed as follows:\n\n    - If NER_Status.ambiguousEntities is empty:\n        - Use details from the input message and chat history to inform the user that no valid match was found. Clearly reference what was attempted or asked, and politely request more specific information to proceed.\n    - If NER_Status.ambiguousEntities is not empty:\n        - Include context from the NER_Status.ambiguousEntities list in your message, summarizing the ambiguous entities for the user’s review. Reference both the user’s current message and recent chat history to clarify what information needs refinement.\n        - Ask the user to provide additional information or clarification to help identify the correct entity.\n        - Only ask for clarification about the ambiguous attributes or entities listed in NER_Status.ambiguousEntities list.\n        - Do not share the ID or Score details with the user.\n        - Do not add anything beyond the context already provided in the input message, the chat history, and the NER_Status.ambiguousEntities list.\n        - Only include suggestions from the NER_Status.ambiguousEntities list, and do not add any suggestions of your own.\n\nIf Ambiguous message is not null:\n    - Use the Ambiguous message user’s current message and recent chat history to clarify what information needs refinement.\n    - Do not share the ID, Score or source details with the user.\n    - Do not add anything beyond the context already provided in the input message, the chat history, and the Ambiguous message\n    - Do not suggest anything other than whats already provided in the Ambiguous message.\n\nAMBIGUOUS ENTITY RESPONSE FORMAT\n\nIf NER_Status.hasNERError is true and NER_Status.ambiguousEntities is not empty, return the response in this structure:\n\nI found multiple possible matches for the entity in your message. Which <entity type> did you mean?\n<option 1 name>\n<option 2 name>\n<option 3 name if present>\n\nPlease specify which of the above is the correct <entity type>.\n\nRules:\n- Use the exact input message text after \"You asked:\".\n- Use the entity value from NER_Status.ambiguousEntities as <entity type>, lowercased for natural wording.\n- List each ambiguous entity name on its own line.\n- Do not include IDs, scores, sources, or extra explanation.\n- Do not combine the options into one sentence.\n\nYou must be polite, concise, and only perform the actions described above. Do not take any actions outside of this prompt. Always leverage both the input message and chat history to construct informative and contextually relevant replies.\nDo not mention the terms NER or Named Entity Resolution in your message to the user.\nDo not ask for information or suggest actions based on details from the input message or chat history. Only ask questions about ambiguous entities.\nDo not comment on your capabilities or explain why you cannot proceed. Be concise and include only the required information.\nIf NER_Status.ambiguousEntities is not empty only ask question to clarify about the ambiguous entity names. No need to add more details."
            }
          ],
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check If BU and Currency Required",
            "returnType": "object",
            "sourceCode": "const intent = $context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_CONTEXT_REWRITER_NODE.$output.workflowCode; \n\nlet result = {\n    \"buAndCurrencyRequired\" : false,\n    \"benefitReviewRequired\" : false\n}\n\nresult.buAndCurrencyRequired = ['program_benefit_flow', 'offers_draft_flow', 'installment_inquiry_flow', 'payments_flow', 'new_cash_calculation_flow', 'email_flow', 'discard_offer_flow','view_draft_flow'].includes(intent);\n\nresult.benefitReviewRequired = ['offers_draft_flow', 'new_cash_calculation_flow', 'email_flow'].includes(intent);\n\nreturn result;"
          },
