              },
              "code": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_PROVIDER_CERT_BASIC_LLAMA_3_3_70B",
              "model": "ORA_LLM_MODEL_GPT_OSS_120B",
              "modelName": "GPT OSS 120B (Basic)",
              "provider": "CERT_BASIC"
            },
            "name": "Get Requested Artifact Details",
            "chatHistoryEnabled": true
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1766052200373"
          },
          "diagram": {
            "x": 8712.5,
            "y": 8368
          },
          "code": "FIN_AP_LLM_GET_REQUESTED_ARTIFACT_DETAILS",
          "convergenceTargetId": "1770716633791",
          "id": "1766132672318",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1766132672319_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "# Objective:\n\nGiven the context: business units list, payment term list, and legal entities list, output a JSON object containing the following fields: businessUnitName, businessUnitId, paymentTerms, legalEntities, and suppliers.\n\n# Instructions:\n  - Contextual Inputs:\n    - User message: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_LLM_CONTEXT_REWRITER_NODE.$output.rewrittenRequest}}\n    - Identified artifact lists:\n        - identifiedBusinessUnits: {{$context.$variables.identifiedBusinessUnits}}\n        - identifiedPaymentTerms: {{$context.$variables.identifiedPaymentTerms}}\n        - identifiedSuppliers: {{$context.$variables.identifiedSuppliers}}\n        - identifiedLegalEntity: {{$context.$variables.identifiedLegalEntities}}\n        - identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts: {{$context.$nodes.FIN_AP_CODE_VERIFY_NER_RESULT.$output.result.ambiguousEntities}}\n    - Default business unit: {{$context.$variables.businessUnitName}}\n    - top N number of Supplliers: {{$context.$variables.topNSuppliers}}\n\n- Priority Rule: Explicit Artifact Type Overrides Name Ambiguity\n\n    - If the latest user message explicitly qualifies a name with an artifact type, that mention must be resolved only as that artifact type.\n    - Explicit qualifiers include:\n        - Business Unit, business unit, BU, businessUnit, BusinessUnit\n        - Supplier\n        - Legal Entity, LE\n        - Payment Term, Term\n\n    - When an explicit artifact type qualifier is present:\n        - Do not create or populate ambiguousMessage for that same name.\n        - Do not treat same-name matches in other artifact lists as ambiguity.\n        - Resolve the artifact using only the matching artifact list, or identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts entries with the same artifact type.\n        - Set requested fields only for the explicitly qualified artifact type.\n        - Set other requested artifact fields to null unless they are separately and explicitly requested.\n\n    - Example:\n        - User message: \"Calculate cash outflow for BU Vision Operations in USD\"\n        - identifiedBusinessUnits contains \"Vision Operations\"\n        - identifiedSuppliers also contains \"Vision Operations\"\n        - identifiedLegalEntities also contains \"Vision Operations\"\n        - Because the user said \"BU Vision Operations\", resolve \"Vision Operations\" as Business Unit only.\n        - requestedBusinessUnit = \"Vision Operations\"\n        - requestedSupplier = null\n        - requestedLegalEntity = null\n        - ambiguousMessage = null\n\n- Determine if the User Query is Business Unit–Specific\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedBusinessUnits and identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts to determine whether the latest query is directed at a specific business unit.\n    - Only consider business units that are explicitly mentioned at least once in the user’s message.\n    - First, check whether the user message contains an explicit business unit type reference such as:\n        - \"Business Unit <name>\"\n        - \"<name> Business Unit\"\n        - \"BU <name>\"\n        - \"businessUnit <name>\"\n        - \"BusinessUnit <name>\"\n    - If the user explicitly specifies that the entity refers to a business unit, treat the entity as a business unit even if the same name appears in other identified artifact lists or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts.\n    - In such cases:\n        - Do not add an entry to ambiguousMessage.\n        - Resolve the entity using identifiedBusinessUnits.\n        - If an exact match is not found, select the closest matching business unit from identifiedBusinessUnits or identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts where entity = \"Business unit\".\n    - Example:\n        - User message: \"How can I optimize payments for Business Unit ABC in currency USD?\"\n        - If identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts contains:\n            - \"ABC Business Unit\"\n            - \"ABC Legal Entity\"\n        - Then resolve the request as:\n            - requestedBusinessUnit = \"ABC Business Unit\"\n    - If multiple business units are explicitly mentioned in the user message:\n        - Set \"moreThanOneBU\" to true.\n        - Set requestedBusinessUnit to null.\n    - If the identified business unit name appears in multiple artifact lists or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts, add ambiguousMessage only when the latest user message does not explicitly qualify that mention as a business unit using terms such as \"BU\", \"Business Unit\", \"business unit\", \"businessUnit\", or \"BusinessUnit\".\n        - Do not treat it as requestedBusinessUnit.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all associated artifact types.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n    - If a valid business unit is identified:\n        - Set requestedBusinessUnit to the resolved business unit name.\n        - Set moreThanOneBU to false.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedBusinessUnit to null.\n        - Set moreThanOneBU to false.\n\n- Determine if the user query is supplier-specific:\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedSuppliers and identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific suppliers.\n    - Only consider suppliers that are explicitly mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - First, check whether the user message contains an explicit supplier type reference such as:\n        - \"Supplier <name>\"\n        - \"<name> Supplier\"\n    - If the user explicitly specifies that the entity refers to a supplier, treat the entity as a supplier even if the same name appears in other identified artifact lists or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts.\n    - In such cases:\n        - Do not add an entry to ambiguousMessage.\n        - Resolve the entity using identifiedSuppliers.\n        - If an exact match is not found, select the closest matching supplier from identifiedSuppliers or identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts where entity = \"Supplier\".\n    - If the identified supplier name appears in multiple artifact lists (besides identifiedSuppliers) or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts and the user has NOT explicitly specified that the entity refers to a supplier:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedSupplier.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all associated artifact types.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n    - If suppliers are identified:\n        - Set requestedSupplier to the detected supplier names.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedSupplier to null.\n    - If the user query is not specific to a single supplier\n        - Example : Show benefit in next 6 weeks if offering dynamic discount for top 5 suppliers by amount payable\n        - set topNSuppliers to the value specified by user.\n        - set the default value as 20 for topNSuppliers if a number is not specified\n        - set the value as 20 for topNSuppliers if the user specifies a value greater than 20.\n\n- Determine if the user query is Legal Entity-specific:\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedLegalEntities and identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific legal entities.\n    - Only consider legal entities that are explicitly mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - First, check whether the user message contains an explicit legal entity type reference such as:\n        - \"Legal Entity <name>\"\n        - \"<name> Legal Entity\"\n    - If the user explicitly specifies that the entity refers to a legal entity, treat the entity as a legal entity even if the same name appears in other identified artifact lists or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts.\n    - In such cases:\n        - Do not add an entry to ambiguousMessage.\n        - Resolve the entity using identifiedLegalEntities.\n        - If an exact match is not found, select the closest matching legal entity from identifiedLegalEntities or identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts where entity = \"Legal Entity\".\n    - If the identified legal entity name appears in multiple artifact lists (besides identifiedLegalEntities) or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts and the user has NOT explicitly specified that the entity refers to a legal entity:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedLegalEntity.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all associated artifact types.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n    - If legal entities are identified:\n        - Set requestedLegalEntity to the detected legal entity names.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedLegalEntity to null.\n\n- Determine if the user query is Payment Term-specific:\n\n    - Review the current user message along with identifiedPaymentTerms and identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts to determine whether the latest query is directed at specific payment terms.\n    - Only consider payment terms that are explicitly mentioned at least once in the user's message.\n    - First, check whether the user message contains an explicit payment term type reference such as:\n        - \"Payment Term <name>\"\n        - \"<name> Payment Term\"\n    - If the user explicitly specifies that the entity refers to a payment term, treat the entity as a payment term even if the same name appears in other identified artifact lists or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts.\n    - In such cases:\n        - Do not add an entry to ambiguousMessage.\n        - Resolve the entity using identifiedPaymentTerms.\n        - If an exact match is not found, select the closest matching payment term from identifiedPaymentTerms or identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts where entity = \"Payment Term\".\n    - If the identified payment term name appears in multiple artifact lists (besides identifiedPaymentTerms) or in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts and the user has NOT explicitly specified that the entity refers to a payment term:\n        - Do not treat it as requestedPaymentTerm.\n        - Add an entry to ambiguousMessage listing all associated artifact types.\n        - Include a justification asking the user to clarify which artifact type should be used.\n    - If payment terms are identified:\n        - Set requestedPaymentTerm to the detected payment term names.\n        - The payment term name may sometimes contain special characters such as _, -, or / within it. Do not trim these characters, and always ensure that you retrieve the full name exactly as provided in the query.\n    - Otherwise:\n        - Set requestedPaymentTerm to null.\n\n\n- Business Unit Extraction:\n\n    - Search the identifiedBusinessUnits list for the business unit name explicitly mentioned in requestedBusinessUnit.\n    - If a match is found in identifiedBusinessUnits:\n        - Set businessUnitName = <Identified business unit name from the identifiedBusinessUnits list>\n        - Retrieve and set businessUnitId for the identified business unit (businessUnitName) from the business units list.\n        - Only select a business unit if it is present in the business units list.\n    - If no match is found in identifiedBusinessUnits:\n        - Search identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts for an artifact where:\n            - entity = \"Business unit\"\n            - name matches the requestedBusinessUnit.\n        - If a matching artifact is found:\n            - Set businessUnitName = <matched business unit name from identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts>\n            - Retrieve and set businessUnitId for the matched business unit from the ambiguous artifacts list.\n            - Only select a business unit if it is present in the ambiguous artifacts list.\n        - Otherwise:\n            - Set businessUnitName = {{$context.$variables.businessUnitName}}\n            - Set businessUnitId = null\n\n\n- Business Unit Filter IDs Extraction:\n\n    - Always return buFilterIds as an array of business unit ID values for all business units explicitly requested in the current user message.\n    - Use identifiedBusinessUnits first. If no matching item is found there, use identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts where entity = \"Business unit\".\n    - Include every resolved business unit ID exactly once, preserving user-requested order when possible.\n    - Convert every ID to a string in the array.\n    - If exactly one business unit is resolved, buFilterIds must contain that one ID and businessUnitId must continue to contain the same ID for legacy compatibility.\n    - If multiple business units are resolved, buFilterIds must contain all resolved IDs. businessUnitName and businessUnitId should use the first resolved business unit only for legacy compatibility.\n    - If no explicit business unit was requested or no business unit ID can be resolved, set buFilterIds to an empty array.\n    - Do not use the default business unit to populate buFilterIds unless the user explicitly asked for that business unit.\n\n\n- Suppliers, Payment Terms, and Legal Entity Extraction:\n\n    - If requestedSuppliers is present and not empty:\n        - Identify matching suppliers in identifiedSuppliers by name.\n        - If no match is found in identifiedSuppliers:\n            - Search identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts for artifacts where entity = \"Supplier\" and name matches the requested supplier name.\n        - If a match is found:\n            - Retrieve the supplier ID from the matched supplier record.\n        - Otherwise:\n            - Return null for suppliers.\n\n    - If requestedPaymentTerms is present and not empty:\n        - Identify matching payment terms in identifiedPaymentTerms by name.\n        - If no match is found in identifiedPaymentTerms:\n            - Search identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts for artifacts where entity = \"Payment Term\" and name matches the requested payment term name.\n        - If a match is found:\n            - Retrieve the payment term ID from the matched payment term record.\n        - Otherwise:\n            - Return null for paymentTerms.\n        - The payment term name may sometimes contain special characters such as _, -, or / within it. Do not trim these characters, and always ensure that you retrieve the full name exactly as provided in the query.\n\n    - If requestedLegalEntities is present and not empty:\n        - Identify matching legal entities in identifiedLegalEntities by name.\n        - If no match is found in identifiedLegalEntities:\n            - Search identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts for artifacts where entity = \"Legal Entity\" and name matches the requested legal entity name.\n        - If a match is found:\n            - Retrieve the legal entity ID from the matched legal entity record.\n        - Otherwise:\n            - Return null for legalEntities.\n\n    - If any requested list is empty or not found, return null for the corresponding field.\n  \n  - Multiple Matches Handling:\n    - If more than one supplier, legal entity, or payment term is matched, list each as an object with both the relevant name and ID in the output array.\n\n- Resolve Ambiguity from identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts:\n\n    - Review identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts against the final selected artifacts from businessUnitName, suppliers, paymentTerms, and legalEntities.\n    - Group the ambiguous artifacts by their shared normalized base identifier or root name.\n      - Example: \"ABC Business Unit\", \"ABC Legal Entity\", and \"Legal ABC Entity\" belong to the same ambiguity group for \"ABC\".\n    - If a final selected artifact matches one ambiguity group and all artifacts in that same group are resolved by the final selection, mark that group as resolved.\n    - If there are no other unresolved ambiguity groups in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts, set resolvedAmbiguityFromList to true.\n    - If one or more other ambiguity groups remain unresolved, set resolvedAmbiguityFromList to false.\n    - Example:\n        - If identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts contains:\n            - \"ABC Business Unit\"\n            - \"ABC Legal Entity\"\n            - \"Legal ABC Entity\"\n          and \"ABC Business Unit\" is selected as the requested artifact:\n            - resolvedAmbiguityFromList = true\n        - If identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts contains:\n            - \"ABC Business Unit\"\n            - \"ABC Legal Entity\"\n            - \"Legal ABC Entity\"\n            - \"CDE Business Unit\"\n            - \"DEF Supplier\"\n          and only \"ABC Business Unit\" is selected as the requested artifact:\n            - resolvedAmbiguityFromList = false\n  \n  - Expected Output Format:\n    - Return only the JSON object in the following structure:\n      {\n        \"suppliers\": [\n          {\n            \"supplierName\": \"<identified supplier name>\",\n            \"supplierId\": <identified supplier id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched supplier)\n        ],\n        \"paymentTerms\": [\n          {\n            \"terms\": \"<identified payment term name>\",\n            \"termsId\": <identified payment term id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched payment term)\n        ],\n        \"legalEntities\": [\n          {\n            \"legalEntityName\": \"<identified legal entity name>\",\n            \"legalEntityId\": <identified legal entity id>\n          }\n          // (repeat for each matched legal entity)\n        ],\n        \"businessUnitName\": \"<business unit name>\",\n        \"businessUnitId\": <business unit id>,\n        \"buFilterIds\": [\"<business unit id>\"]\n      }\n\n# Important:\n\n- Output only the JSON object above, with no explanatory text or formatting.\n- If a section has no matches, the respective field should be set to null or an empty array, as appropriate.\n- Do not add an entry to ambiguousMessage if no matching artifact candidate was found in identifiedAmbiguousArtifacts for the requested entity type."
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"businessUnitName\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n\"moreThanOneBU\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"businessUnitId\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"paymentTerms\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"legalEntities\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"suppliers\": {\n            \"type\": \"list\"\n        },\n        \"requestedBusinessUnit\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedSupplier\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedLegalEntity\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"requestedPaymentTerm\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"ambiguousMessage\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"resolvedAmbiguityFromList\": {\n             \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n        \"buFilterIds\": {\n              \"type\": \"list\"\n         },\n        \"topNSuppliers\": {\n              \"type\": \"integer\"\n         }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
